id=08
title=COMMUNICATIONS LINE SELECTOR
objective=Restore transmission source selection.
hint=The routing switch chooses which signal reaches Y.
briefing=The transmitter receives one of two binary data signals. When the route selector is OFF, output Y must copy the primary signal A. When the selector is ON, output Y must copy backup signal C. Changes to the unselected signal must have no effect on Y.

input_A=Primary communications data
input_B=Route selector: OFF for primary, ON for backup
input_C=Backup communications data
output_description=Data transmitted to the communications uplink

